// XFAIL: RT-448: UNSOUND: `fn ki<T: Into<&'static i64>>(x: T) -> &'static i64 { x.into() }` called as `ki(&v[0])`, then `drop(v)` and a read of the result, is accepted: the 'static that `&i64: Into<&'static i64>` needs (through std's blanket `impl<T, U: From<T>> Into<U> for T` and the reflexive `From<T> for T`) is lost, and the read is a use after free; rustc E0597 (`v` does not live long enough) (0.30.2)
// From the review of g302fnval (its form s33e_into_direct_only). Since
// v0.30.1 at least (the same use after free). The g302bor2 round-2 build
// refuses it. The fn-value form, `v.first().map(ki::<&i64>)`, is
// rt_448b. RT-267 is a result tied to its argument only by a blanket
// Into bound; RT-308/364/421 the 'static bound of a fn used as a value.
// FLAGS: --check-alloc
// ERROR: line 16
fn ki<T: Into<&'static i64>>(x: T) -> &'static i64 {
    x.into()
}

fn main(gpa: Gpa) {
    let mut v: Vec<i64, Gpa> = Vec::new_in(gpa);
    v.push(1000);
    let a = ki(&v[0]);
    drop(v);
    println("{}", a);
}
